PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- The chemical probe is a Cy5-conjugated HaloTag ligand (630 nm), which selectively labels the HaloTag-eGFP fusion protein in neutrophils driven by the lyz promoter.
- In a zebrafish tailfin injury assay, neutrophils are the first responders, arriving at the wound site well before mpeg1-expressing macrophages (559 nm).
- Explicit protocol instructions to grow larvae in the dark until 4 dpf preserve the synthetic Cy5 fluorophore against photobleaching, confirming that the labeled neutrophil cohort remains detectable alongside constitutively expressed eGFP (488 nm).
- The initial fluorescent signals detected at the wound margin will therefore arise concurrently from both 630 nm and 488 nm excitation, firmly supporting Choice D.
}

